+    *   Ground truth image $I \in \mathbb{R}^{H \times W \times 3}$.
+    *   Camera parameters for back-projection.
+    *   Global appearance embedding $l \in \mathbb{R}^A$ for the current view.
+    *   Multi-resolution hash grids $\{G_i\}_{i=0}^{L-1}$ storing local spatial features.
+    *   Lightweight MLP $f$ parameters.
 *   **Outputs:**
-    *   Transformed image $I_t$ used for loss computation.
-    *   Optimized Gaussian attributes and appearance module parameters (hash grid features, MLP weights, view embeddings).
