-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Blotchy Surfaces:** Without identity regularization ($L_{ID}$), Gaussian primitives tend to adjust their colors instead of the appearance model, causing blotchy homogeneous surfaces [S1].
-*   **Unpleasant Colors:** Lack of regularization can lead to unpleasant colors in the reconstructed scene [S1].
-*   **Performance:** Querying the appearance model for every pixel is time-consuming; the cell-based query is necessary to minimize optimization time [S1].
-*   **Depth Accuracy:** The method relies on mean depth calculated during differentiable rasterization for back-projection [S1].
